  "title": "Peter B NDE 4610",
  "date": "3/5/2010",
  "content": "My first experience was a feeling of floating. I didn't see my body, but I knew that I was not in my body. On my right, there was the sound of a large crowd, voices that were so numerous, I couldn't tell if I knew anyone, but it sounded like a happy party. A tall wall separated me from everyone. To my left, I saw a tunnel of a sort, the walls seemed to be turning and I was slowly being drawn into it, not quite sure if I was supposed to go into it. Eventually I started down the tunnel and saw a brilliant light that glowed so bright, that I couldn't see a face but a silhouette of a man. I knew he was the Lord. As I started to get closer, I felt a sudden pulling on my feet and was rushed backward. The tunnel spun faster and before I knew it, I was in the emergency room and told my wife right away that I had seen the Lord and I was in heaven. She immediately acknowledged that she believed me because she had found me outside, blue in color and not breathing. She said that she knew I was gone, but had fallen on top of me and prayed that the Lord would let me come back, that she wasn't ready for me to go, and in the witness of our neighbor who is a retired intensive care unit nurse, I began to breathe. By the time the ambulance arrived, I was breathing very heavily on my own and no one ever did rescue breathing or car.",
